From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] skw: ask for a board's own firmware without a failure logged

A board-named firmware file is optional: the driver falls back to the
generic one when it is absent. Requested as any other, its absence logs
"Direct firmware load ... failed" though the radio loads. Ask for it with
firmware_request_nowarn(), the generic file as before.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/include/linux/skw_firmware_helper.h b/include/linux/skw_firmware_helper.h
--- a/include/linux/skw_firmware_helper.h
+++ b/include/linux/skw_firmware_helper.h
@@ -53,6 +53,21 @@
 }
 
 /*
+ * A file the caller falls back from: absent, it is no failure worth a log line.
+ */
+static inline int skw_firmware_request_optional(const struct firmware **fw,
+						const char *name,
+						struct device *dev,
+						int direct)
+{
+#if LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(4, 17, 0)
+	return firmware_request_nowarn(fw, name, dev);
+#else
+	return skw_firmware_request_one(fw, name, dev, direct);
+#endif
+}
+
+/*
  * Request a firmware file with optional subdirectory and board-specific
  * fallback.  If @firmware_dir is set, look under that subdirectory.  If
  * @board_id is set, first try name.<board_id>.ext, then name.ext.
@@ -113,7 +128,7 @@
 
 	if (board_name) {
 		pr_info("skw firmware: request board firmware %s\n", board_name);
-		ret = skw_firmware_request_one(fw, board_name, dev, direct);
+		ret = skw_firmware_request_optional(fw, board_name, dev, direct);
 		if (!ret) {
 			pr_info("skw firmware: loaded board firmware %s\n", board_name);
 			kfree(full_name);
